From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neogram Patchset <patches@neogram.invalid>
Subject: feature/prefer-ipv6: prefer IPv6 for connections to Telegram

Behind NeoOptions.PREFER_IPV6. When the device has an IPv6 address, ConnectionsManager.getIpStrategy answers IPv6 only, as it does when the server config sets force_try_ipv6; that server flag is rewritten on every config update, so the option cannot simply set it. Changing the option makes every active account reconnect (checkConnection).
---
 TMessagesProj/src/main/java/org/telegram/tgnet/ConnectionsManager.java | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/TMessagesProj/src/main/java/org/telegram/tgnet/ConnectionsManager.java b/TMessagesProj/src/main/java/org/telegram/tgnet/ConnectionsManager.java
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/TMessagesProj/src/main/java/org/telegram/tgnet/ConnectionsManager.java
+++ b/TMessagesProj/src/main/java/org/telegram/tgnet/ConnectionsManager.java
@@ -1154,7 +1154,7 @@ public class ConnectionsManager extends BaseController {
                 }
             }
             if (hasIpv6) {
-                if (forceTryIpV6) {
+                if (forceTryIpV6 || ru.llacker.neogram.NeoNetwork.preferIpv6()) {
                     return USE_IPV6_ONLY;
                 }
                 if (hasStrangeIpv4) {
